  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The only possible values of \\(X\\) are 0 and 1, with \\(P(X=1)=1/4\\). What is \\(P(X=0)\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "3/4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Since 0 and 1 are the only possible values of \\(X\\), the events \\(X=0\\) and \\(X=1\\) are complementary. Therefore,\n\\[\nP(X=0)=1-P(X=1)=1-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n\\]",
